["q-69650/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26e8a6ff-e5ed-59a7-b31d-1981495bf26a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-69650"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-317367/field-1/2975d51709004513603edea75e6b4a3b80948e01184836d4d575ed4097167ce1" :answer/id #uuid "f36c7948-18b7-54c5-b13a-279894f0c0fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317367/field-1/f6c9d50fedf74e2b4ac0a2ef4f0295074416c004a23e123233fa99180084a57f" :answer/id #uuid "40851764-fbe7-5355-ad9b-a183ae609e77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{23}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317367/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2059530f-c1cf-5946-90cf-92510df047fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317367/field-1/2975d51709004513603edea75e6b4a3b80948e01184836d4d575ed4097167ce1" :answer-field/choices ["q-317367/field-1/2975d51709004513603edea75e6b4a3b80948e01184836d4d575ed4097167ce1" "q-317367/field-1/f6c9d50fedf74e2b4ac0a2ef4f0295074416c004a23e123233fa99180084a57f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317367" :question/id #uuid "4303d5e5-45e5-500e-bd51-baaa5d0f753a" :question/math-academy-id "q-317367" :question/problem "Calculate $det(D)$ given that\n$D=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5} & -3 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(D)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5} & -3 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-317367/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26e8a6ff-e5ed-59a7-b31d-1981495bf26a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317367"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-317372/field-1/9be6bb25a43f958d7eaef43d56198935d8a7d19c93a72859ed8920624e59b294" :answer/id #uuid "661ed604-fc38-5610-8d0a-75839dfcbaa7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x^2+10y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317372/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "570b9551-cc35-5441-ae59-94fd02944893" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317372/field-1/9be6bb25a43f958d7eaef43d56198935d8a7d19c93a72859ed8920624e59b294" :answer-field/choices ["q-317372/field-1/9be6bb25a43f958d7eaef43d56198935d8a7d19c93a72859ed8920624e59b294"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317372" :question/id #uuid "ec791774-0f47-524b-8822-8346fd1d9cbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-317372" :question/problem "Calculate $det(D)$ given that\n$D=[\\begin{aligned}3x & 2y \\\\ -5 & x\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(D)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}3x & 2y \\\\ -5 & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3x\\cdot x-2y\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+10y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-317372/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26e8a6ff-e5ed-59a7-b31d-1981495bf26a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317372"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275601/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "f2b207fc-6102-500d-b8f7-9efc0529f154" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275601/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "03e5b773-3b84-5980-91eb-d0d143a88973" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275601/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4308871e-50d2-53f5-922e-ff5a2793695f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275601/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-275601/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-275601/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275601" :question/id #uuid "875eb3e3-fc69-5562-b815-beb92eb0cf4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-275601" :question/problem "If\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3+p & 4p-{p}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5-p\\end{aligned}]$\nand $det(A)=7,$ what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}3+p & 4p-{p}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5-p\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3+p)(5-p)-(4p-{p}^{2})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =15-3p+5p-{p}^{2}-4p+{p}^{2} \\\\  & =15-2p-\\cancel{{p}^{2}}+\\cancel{{p}^{2}} \\\\  & =15-2p.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $det(A)=7$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =7 \\\\ 15-2p & =7 \\\\ -2p & =-8 \\\\ p & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-275601/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ccdde46-a4ab-517e-910b-571a3a166b6a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275601"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11653/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "185c55d3-c326-5aea-9adb-2633dde5da92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value